  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Alert 943 Displacement in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project titled &quot;Provision of emergency basic lifesaving WASH, Health, Nutrition, and Protection services&quot; is set in Payume and Kendila Payams of Morobo County, Central Equatoria State, South Sudan. It aims to deliver critical interventions in Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), Health, Nutrition, and Protection, targeting vulnerable populations affected by crisis. The implementing agency, an international organization with strong local presence and experience, plans to execute the project through direct implementation and partnerships with both pre-existing and new CSOs/NGOs. The initiative addresses urgent humanitarian needs in a conflict-affected and underserved region.</narrative>
  </description>
